{{wikipedia}}
{{also|diploïd}}
==English==

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{cytology}} Of a cell, having a pair of each type of [[chromosome]], one of the pair being derived from the [[ovum]] and the other from the [[spermatozoon]]. Most [[somatic cell]]s of higher organisms are diploid.

====Derived terms====
* [[diploidy]]

